  "aboutAppPageTitle": "About the app",
  "aboutChurchFocusedP1": "Public platforms such as YouTube and others are valuable channels for sharing content. However, they also offer many items unrelated to the life or mission of the Church. When a believer searches for a sermon or hymn, they can quickly be exposed to other videos, recommendations, and content that may distract them.",
  "aboutChurchFocusedP2": "This app was therefore designed to offer a digital space more focused on the Church's resources. Members come with a clear purpose and find the content meant for them directly, without browsing an environment filled with unrelated material.",
  "aboutChurchFocusedP3": "This approach is especially important for young people and children, but it also benefits every believer who wants to devote their digital time to the Church's teachings, worship, and resources.",
  "aboutChurchFocusedTitle": "A space focused on Church life",
  "aboutContinuityP1": "This app does not replace the website or the Church's other communication platforms. It complements existing tools by offering an experience suited to everyday smartphone use.",
  "aboutContinuityP2": "It helps bring members closer to Church life, including those who cannot be physically present at a service because of work obligations, distance, or any other circumstance.",
  "aboutContinuityP3": "Through this app, we wanted technology to serve an essential goal: making access to the Word, teachings, and Church life easier, everywhere and at any time.",
  "aboutContinuityTitle": "Continuity between the Church and its members",
  "aboutDeveloperServiceP1": "This app is the result of a development effort aimed at offering members a tool that is simple, accessible, modern, and useful.",
  "aboutDeveloperServiceP2": "As developers, our aim is not simply to create yet another app, but to put our technical skills at the service of a vision: using today's digital tools to make the Church's communication easier and, at our level, to help spread God's Word.",
  "aboutDeveloperServiceP3": "May this tool be useful to brothers and sisters, make access to the Church's resources easier, and help maintain their connection with the community, wherever they are.",
  "aboutDeveloperServiceTitle": "Built to serve the Church",
  "aboutLibraryP1": "For many years, Shekinah Tabernacle has made the Message available to believers through the Kosher program on computer and USB drives distributed in the Church. These familiar tools have helped countless believers and preachers study, meditate on, and preach the Word in many different settings.",
  "aboutLibraryP2": "The app's Library extends this same approach to the smartphone. It offers believers convenient access to Golden Nuggets and publications, but above all it meets the needs of preachers, who can now carry the Message with them everywhere — while traveling, visiting, in meetings, or in places where a computer or USB drive is not available.",
  "aboutLibraryP3": "Messages can be downloaded for offline reading, with a reader suited to studying the Word. What Kosher and USB media already provide at the desk or in the pulpit, the Library now puts in your pocket, for personal edification and ministry alike.",
  "aboutLibraryTitle": "The Library: carrying the Message on mobile",
  "aboutWhyDeveloper": "Developed by Brother Jean Malonga, a believer and member of Shekinah Tabernacle, this app was designed to meet the practical needs of the faithful in our assembly.",
  "aboutWhyIntro": "This app was built on a simple conviction: technology can serve the spread of God's Word and fellowship among the members of the Church.",
  "aboutWhyP1": "Today, the Church already has several means of communication, including its website and digital platforms, to share sermons, worship services, hymns, announcements, and the Church's various activities. These tools play an important role in communication and the edification of believers.",
  "aboutWhyP2": "However, access to this content is not always as simple as it could be. Many members have a smartphone but are not necessarily comfortable browsing the Internet or carrying out the steps needed to find a sermon, join a live service, or watch a teaching again.",
  "aboutWhyP3": "To meet this reality, this mobile app dedicated to the Church was developed: to give members simple, direct, and organized access to the Church's content and activities from their smartphone.",
  "aboutWhyP4": "The app makes it easy to find live worship services, sermons, teachings, hymns, schedules, announcements, and other spiritual resources. It also helps members receive important information through notifications, such as worship times, the start of a live stream, or newly available content.",
  "aboutWhyTitle": "Why this app?",
