  "branhamAngelVisitP1": "The visions continued. Fellow ministers told him his visions did not come from God. This troubled him deeply. The burden became too heavy; he went into the wilderness to seek God's will. There, in an old trapper's cabin, the Angel of the Lord gave him his commission: \"If you can get the people to believe you, and be sincere when you pray, nothing shall stand before your prayers, not even cancer.\"",
  "branhamAngelVisitP2": "All doubts were gone. Now he had a commission, and he went forward with confidence.",
  "branhamBaptistCaption": "Like John the Baptist, the prophet was confirmed in the waters of baptism.",
  "branhamBaptistQuote": "\"As John was sent with a Message for the first coming, this is likewise the second Message for the second coming.\"",
  "branhamBeginningP1": "Dawn was just breaking through the cool April sky. The single wooden window opened to let morning light into the tiny one-room cabin. Inside, young Charles Branham put his hands in his brand-new overalls and looked at his 15-year-old wife. \"We'll call him William,\" said the father.",
  "branhamBeginningP2": "A supernatural Light entered through the window. The Light moved through the room and stopped above the bed where the newborn lay. It was the same Light that had led the Hebrew children out of Egypt. The same Light that had met Paul on the road to Damascus. And it would now lead this child destined to call the Bride of Christ out of the world. This Light was none other than the Angel of the Lord, the Pillar of Fire: it had appeared to man once again.",
  "branhamBeginningP3": "\"And there, in that little log cabin on the morning of April 6, the midwife opened the window to let in the light so Mom and Dad could see how I was. That's when a Light the size of a pillow swirled in through the window. It circled around where I was and came down on the bed. Several mountain people stood there. They were weeping.\"",
  "branhamBeginningP4": "The humble home stood in the hills of southern Kentucky, near the small town of Burkesville. It was April 6, 1909. The baby was the first of ten children born to Charles and Ella Branham.",
  "branhamBeginningQuote": "\"When I was born in a little cabin back there in Kentucky, the Angel of the Lord came in the window and stood there. It was a Pillar of Fire.\"",
  "branhamClosingQuote": "\"A great prophet has appeared among us, and God has visited His people.\"",
  "branhamClosingRef": "Luke 7:16",
  "branhamDoctrineP1": "His teachings and doctrines, strictly based on the Holy Scriptures—the Bible, which he recognized as the sole authority of faith—showed that the Lord Jesus Christ, supreme Deity, is the only true God made flesh, and that His Name, Jesus Christ, is the only true Name among men for salvation; that faith in Him alone brings Eternal Life, and that the only biblical baptism is by immersion in the Name of the Lord Jesus Christ.",
  "branhamFactBirth": "Born April 6, 1909 in Burkesville, Kentucky (USA)",
  "branhamFactMalachi": "Prophet of Malachi 4:5-6 — preparing the Bride for the Rapture",
  "branhamFactMinistry": "Healing campaigns, visions, and miracles confirmed by thousands of witnesses",
  "branhamFactPhoto": "Pillar of Fire photograph authenticated by George J. Lacy (FBI expert), 1950",
  "branhamHeaderSummary": "A prophet confirmed by God for our generation, bearing the end-time Message and supernatural signs.",
  "branhamHealingRevivalP1": "Hundreds of thousands attended Branham campaigns. Thousands were healed in the Name of the Lord Jesus Christ. Other evangelists, such as Oral Roberts, T. L. Osborn, and A. A. Allen, soon followed Brother Branham and began their own healing revival campaigns.",
  "branhamHoustonQuote": "\"I cannot heal anyone. Here is what I can say. When I was born in the state of Kentucky, a Light entered the room of that little shelter where I was. Since that time, It has been with me. It is an Angel of God. Throughout my life, He told me things that came to pass, and I spoke them exactly as He told me. And I challenge anyone anywhere to show me one statement made in the Name of the Lord that did not come to pass exactly as announced.\"",
  "branhamIntroP1": "In this end time, God has visited this last generation in an extraordinary way through the prophetic ministry of His servant William Marrion Branham. Born April 6, 1909 in Burkesville, Kentucky, USA, his remarkable life was marked by supernatural phenomena: visions and prophecies (always fulfilled), angelic appearances, miraculous healings, raising of the dead, and more. William Marrion Branham is truly a prophet sent by Almighty God with signs and wonders to prepare the people for the Rapture before the great and terrible day of God's judgment, as announced and promised.",
  "branhamPillarP1": "Brother Branham often described a Pillar of Fire that confirmed his ministry. It was present at his birth, seen by thousands on the banks of the Ohio River, and seemed to follow him wherever he went.",
  "branhamPillarP2": "In 1950, the Lord gave believers and unbelievers alike infallible proof that this Pillar of Fire accompanied the prophet. The evening at Sam Houston Coliseum was surrounded by controversy: a debate on Divine healing pitted Reverend F. F. Bosworth against a skeptical pastor.",
  "branhamPillarP3": "Brother Bosworth demonstrated the authenticity of healing with biblical proof, then asked all who had been healed to stand. Thousands stood. The skeptic issued this challenge: \"Let this Divine healer come forward. Let him perform.\"",
  "branhamPillarP4": "Brother Bosworth invited Brother Branham to the platform. Filled with the Holy Spirit, the prophet gave this response:",
  "branhamPillarP5": "After these words, the Holy Spirit came upon the platform; the photographer took a picture. On that final photograph was the Pillar of Fire in visible form, suspended above the head of God's prophet, William Marrion Branham. Brother Branham declared: \"God will bear witness. I will add nothing.\"",
  "branhamPillarP6": "The photograph was submitted to George J. Lacy, professional document examiner for the FBI, who confirmed the photograph's authenticity as an expert.",
  "branhamPillarWitnessQuote": "\"The children of Israel witnessed the Pillar of Fire that led Moses, and today people have witnessed that same Pillar of Fire leading another prophet.\"",
  "branhamScriptureHoseaQuote": "\"By a prophet the Lord brought Israel up out of Egypt, and by a prophet Israel was preserved.\"",
  "branhamScriptureHoseaRef": "Hosea 12:13",
  "branhamScriptureMalachiQuote": "\"Behold, I will send you Elijah the prophet before the coming of the great and dreadful day of the Lord. And he shall turn the heart of the children to their fathers, lest I come and smite the earth with a curse.\"",
  "branhamScriptureMalachiRef": "Malachi 4:5-6",
