  "branhamTitle": "William Marrion Branham",
  "branhamVisionsP1": "As a child, the Angel spoke to him for the first time, saying he would live near a town called New Albany. Two years later, his family moved to Jeffersonville, Indiana, just a few kilometers from New Albany. A few years later, the Angel spoke again to the young prophet. On a quiet September day, the boy sat in the shade of a large poplar tree. Suddenly a Voice spoke: \"Don't drink, don't smoke, and don't defile your body in any way; you will have a work to do when you are older.\" Frightened, the seven-year-old dropped his buckets and ran to his mother.",
  "branhamVisionsP2": "The Lord gave him visions of the future. And as with the prophets before him, the visions never failed.",
  "branhamYouthIntro": "Throughout his life, Brother Branham longed to be in wild places. At 18, he left Indiana for the rugged mountains of the West. His stay in Arizona was short, however, as he was forced to return.",
  "branhamYouthQuote": "\"One day I decided I had found a way to get rid of that call: I would go West to work on a ranch. My friend, God is just as great out there as anywhere. May you learn from my experience. When He calls you, answer Him.\" He went to Arizona fleeing the God of Love, but ranch life could not satisfy his soul. After his brother Edward's death, God dealt with him again. Dear reader, when He calls, answer Him.",
