  "fondationLabel": "Fondation Shekinah",
  "fondationMessageNations": "The Message for the nations",
  "fondationMessageNationsP1": "A major prophet sent according to biblical promises, brother Branham was aware that his Message had to travel the world and reach the most remote corners of our planet.",
  "fondationMessageNationsP2": "At the Lord's recommendation, he showed great concern that the Message, the end-time gospel, be spread in the form of tapes, brochures, and books to serve as a testimony to all nations.",
  "fondationScriptureQuote": "« Oh that my words were written! Oh that they were inscribed in a book! Oh that with an iron stylus and lead they were engraved in the rock forever!... »",
  "fondationScriptureRef": "Job 19:23-24",
  "fondationTitle": "Fondation Shekinah",
  "fondationWordForAll": "The Word for all",
  "fondationWordForAllP1": "God's will is that all people come to the knowledge of the Truth which is His Word. For it is the Word that sets them free and sanctifies them. Did He not say that My people perish for lack of knowledge?",
  "fondationWordForAllP2": "When God gave the law to Moses, He wrote it Himself on tablets which He then entrusted to His prophet to bring to the people.",
  "fondationWrittenWord": "The written Word through the ages",
  "fondationWrittenWordP1": "Jeremiah received a message from God and Baruch, his secretary, wrote it down so it could be read to the people. In His time, the Lord Jesus chose twelve apostles to spread the message, and some among them and other men called by God wrote down His Words and His Life so they would be carried to all future generations.",
  "fondationWrittenWordP2": "After his conversion and call to ministry, Paul himself wrote the Lord's commandments to the Church in the form of letters.",
